00:17:45,440 --> 00:17:46,320
Chill, Kageyama!

275
00:17:46,720 --> 00:17:48,440
What are you talking about?

276
00:17:49,060 --> 00:17:51,560
As the name suggests, Kageyama, but chill!

277
00:17:54,380 --> 00:17:54,940
Remember?

278
00:17:55,460 --> 00:17:58,500
It's like when I pulled off a quick attack without closing my eyes!

279
00:18:00,080 --> 00:18:02,380
Or when he got Tsukishima to jump higher!

280
00:18:02,820 --> 00:18:04,280
I sensed it in him then, too!

281
00:18:05,220 --> 00:18:08,300
It's basically when he's at the very top of his entire game!

282
00:18:08,740 --> 00:18:11,300
That said, it's only his face that's calm.

283
00:18:11,440 --> 00:18:14,440
Inside, he's as brutal as ever, so you must proceed with caution!

284
00:18:14,860 --> 00:18:17,860
This mode often activates when he's confronting a powerful foe!

285
00:18:18,340 --> 00:18:20,420
He sounded like an instruction manual there!

286
00:18:22,660 --> 00:18:25,620
I can feel the electricity in the air!

287
00:18:25,620 --> 00:18:26,740
Huh?

288
00:18:29,080 --> 00:18:31,200
Inatisaki is calling their first time out!

289
00:18:31,660 --> 00:18:33,800
We've seen some powerful serves today, Phil!

290
00:18:34,140 --> 00:18:37,520
Yes, both schools have shown a wide array of strong attacks!

291
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:42,140
Just keep pressing the attack like you have been the whole set, but don't slack on your receipts!

292
00:18:42,140 --> 00:18:44,680
I'm sure you're all getting tired, but I promise they are, too!

293
00:18:44,900 --> 00:18:46,680
Things are working in our favor right now!

294
00:18:47,360 --> 00:18:50,020
Could Kageyama's serves be the beginning of a Karashino comeback?

295
00:18:50,020 --> 00:18:51,340
Just keep concentrating!

296
00:18:51,340 --> 00:18:52,000
Yes, sir!

297
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:05,540
Yes!

298
00:19:06,820 --> 00:19:08,180
He scores again!

299
00:19:08,560 --> 00:19:09,900
That time it's a good one!

300
00:19:09,900 --> 00:19:11,580
I'm not in front of his concentration!

301
00:19:11,580 --> 00:19:12,140
Food!

302
00:19:12,140 --> 00:19:19,980
One more time!

303
00:19:21,240 --> 00:19:21,760
Get in!

304
00:19:22,740 --> 00:19:23,180
Alan!

305
00:19:25,120 --> 00:19:31,600
We may not be able to crush their spirits, but if we can annoy them just a little, if we

306
00:19:31,600 --> 00:19:35,180
can get them to hit their spikes just a little more aggressively...

307
00:19:35,180 --> 00:19:35,800
Left, left!

308
00:19:36,080 --> 00:19:37,100
Three blockers!

309
00:19:37,100 --> 00:19:51,380
We have a chance!

310
00:19:51,560 --> 00:19:53,200
We can turn this around!

311
00:19:54,700 --> 00:19:56,460
Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes, yes!

312
00:19:56,500 --> 00:19:57,580
That's what I'm talking about!

313
00:19:57,680 --> 00:19:57,920
Yeah!

314
00:19:58,260 --> 00:20:00,360
Oh, hey, so does that mean...

315
00:20:00,360 --> 00:20:00,920
Exactly.

316
00:20:01,860 --> 00:20:03,280
I was not a good out.

317
00:20:03,280 --> 00:20:06,200
Go, go, Karasuno!

318
00:20:06,580 --> 00:20:08,000
Go, go, Karasuno!

319
00:20:12,440 --> 00:20:13,100
Damn it!

320
00:20:13,100 --> 00:20:15,920
And the ball is sailing right back over to Karasuno's side!

321
00:20:20,780 --> 00:20:21,820
Too fast!

322
00:20:24,820 --> 00:20:26,660
Don't go getting a big head now.

323
00:20:28,880 --> 00:20:29,480
Summon!

324
00:20:29,480 --> 00:20:30,480
Yeah!

325
00:20:34,140 --> 00:20:36,740
This time it's Alan Ojiro getting the point!

326
00:20:37,060 --> 00:20:39,280
He's making his presence known as an ace!

327
00:20:39,540 --> 00:20:42,820
That was an impressive dig from Atsumu as well!

328
00:20:43,040 --> 00:20:48,680
Tobio Kageyama and Atsumu-mia are both excellent setters and candidates for the All Japan Youth

329
00:20:48,680 --> 00:20:49,040
Team.

330
00:20:49,260 --> 00:20:53,060
But as you can see, they don't have to be putting up sets for the sparks to fly.

331
00:20:53,480 --> 00:20:54,080
Osamu!

332
00:20:54,280 --> 00:20:55,980
Hurry up and finish this set already!

333
00:20:55,980 --> 00:20:59,400
Also, I want to point out, I got way more aces than you today!

334
00:20:59,620 --> 00:21:00,960
Would you please shut up?

335
00:21:06,340 --> 00:21:07,320
Well, shit.

336
00:21:12,140 --> 00:21:14,180
He might have hit that one a bit too hard!

337
00:21:14,300 --> 00:21:15,800
It's way out of bounds, filth!

338
00:21:15,980 --> 00:21:16,860
No way!

339
00:21:16,940 --> 00:21:17,520
That flew?

340
00:21:18,180 --> 00:21:20,220
That is not where the ball goes!

341
00:21:20,600 --> 00:21:21,380
Yeah, right.

342
00:21:21,800 --> 00:21:23,440
Like you've never done that before.

343
00:21:23,540 --> 00:21:25,180
You just had to provoke him, didn't you?

344
00:21:25,180 --> 00:21:25,680
Ah!

345
00:21:26,860 --> 00:21:30,460
Osamu seems super chill, but he can still be pretty competitive sometimes.

346
00:21:30,520 --> 00:21:31,100
Of course.

347
00:21:31,500 --> 00:21:32,760
Just consider his brother.

348
00:21:34,080 --> 00:21:34,560
Oh.

349
00:21:36,280 --> 00:21:38,940
Shake up their psyches, even the tiniest bit.

350
00:21:39,400 --> 00:21:42,020
And it'll throw off their plays ever so slightly.

351
00:21:43,060 --> 00:21:43,540
It's in!

352
00:21:43,540 --> 00:21:45,840
All those little irregularities start to build up.

353
00:21:46,180 --> 00:21:46,460
Gen!

354
00:21:46,460 --> 00:21:58,480
And then, the tide turns.

355
00:22:04,800 --> 00:22:05,280
Sorry.

356
00:22:05,520 --> 00:22:06,000
All good.

357
00:22:06,180 --> 00:22:07,020
No worries, Asahi.

358
00:22:07,520 --> 00:22:08,520
I'm sorry, guys.

359
00:22:08,600 --> 00:22:09,540
Hey, we'll get all rhythm back.

360
00:22:09,620 --> 00:22:10,940
Just try to stay calm.

361
00:22:10,940 --> 00:22:11,780
Oh, what?

362
00:22:11,860 --> 00:22:12,560
Oh!

363
00:22:12,840 --> 00:22:12,880
Huh?

364
00:22:12,880 --> 00:22:42,860
I don't know.

365
00:22:42,880 --> 00:23:12,860
I don't know.

366
00:23:12,880 --> 00:23:42,860
I don't know.

367
00:23:42,880 --> 00:24:12,860
I don't know.

